help: the trait `structio::json::Read<'_>` is not implemented for `Register`
  --> tests/ui/no_read_impl.rs:6:1
   |
 6 | struct Register(u32);
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: a type becomes readable by being declared with `structio::object!` or `#[derive(Structio)]`, or by a `json::Read` impl written by hand
   = note: a declaration generates both directions unless it narrows to one: a struct that is only ever written is declared `object!(write_only ..)` or `#[structio(write_only)]`, and then nothing in it needs a read impl
   = note: where the struct really is read, a stub whose body is `p.skip_value()` is legitimate there
   = help: the following other types implement trait `structio::json::Read<'de>`:
             &'de str
             ()
             (A, B)
             (A, B, C)
             (A, B, C, D)
             (A, B, C, D, E)
             (A, B, C, D, E, F)
             (A, B, C, D, E, F, G)
           and $N others
   = note: this error originates in the macro `$crate::__json_read_impls` which comes from the expansion of the macro `structio::object` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)

